---
import Service from '../layouts/Service.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import YouTubeVideo from '../components/YouTubeVideo.astro';
import { videos } from '../data/videos';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What does TimberTech Platinum Pro mean?', a: 'Platinum Pro is TimberTech’s top contractor level. It means TC Decks is trained and certified on TimberTech products, and it lets us offer TimberTech labor and material warranty coverage on top of our own 7-year workmanship warranty.' },
  { q: 'Which TimberTech line should I choose?', a: 'It depends on the look you want and your budget. Prime+, Premier and Terrain are solid entry lines; Harvest, Landmark and Reserve step up in color and grain; Legacy and Vintage are the premium collections with the richest look. We bring samples so you can see them in your own light.' },
  { q: 'Is TimberTech PVC better than composite?', a: 'TimberTech Advanced PVC (the AZEK-made lines) is fully synthetic, very light, stays cooler than traditional composite and holds up to moisture extremely well. Capped composite is a great value. Both are low maintenance; we will walk you through the trade-offs for your deck.' },
  { q: 'Do you build TimberTech decks in Salt Lake County too?', a: 'Yes. We build across Utah County and Salt Lake County, from Saratoga Springs, Lehi and Highland to Draper, Sandy and South Jordan.' },
];
---
<Service
  slug="timbertech-decks"
  name="TimberTech Decks"
  title="TimberTech Deck Builder in Utah | Platinum Pro | TC Decks"
  description="TimberTech Platinum Pro deck builder in Utah County and Salt Lake County. Custom TimberTech PVC and composite decks with a 7-year workmanship warranty."
  h1="TimberTech decks from a Platinum Pro"
  lead="TimberTech is our first choice for most decks. As a TimberTech Platinum Pro, we install it the way TimberTech intends and can offer manufacturer labor and material coverage on top of our own 7-year workmanship warranty."
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Why we lead with TimberTech</h2>
  <p>We have built with almost every decking brand on the market. TimberTech is the one we recommend most often for Utah homes, for a few reasons:</p>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li><strong>Built for high-altitude sun.</strong> Capped boards resist fading and staining, which matters at Utah elevations.</li>
    <li><strong>Handles freeze-thaw.</strong> The boards don't soak up water, so they don't swell, split or rot through our winters.</li>
    <li><strong>Cooler options.</strong> TimberTech Advanced PVC lines stay noticeably cooler underfoot than traditional composite on a west-facing deck.</li>
    <li><strong>Colors that look like real wood.</strong> Multi-tonal colors such as English Walnut, French White Oak and Pecan read as natural wood from a few feet away.</li>
  </ul>

  <Photo src="/images/projects/highland-english-walnut-hideaway/highland-timbertech-vintage-english-walnut-timber-pavilion" alt="TimberTech Vintage English Walnut deck under a timber pavilion in Highland, Utah" />

  <h2>What being a Platinum Pro means for you</h2>
  <p>TimberTech Platinum Pro is TimberTech’s highest contractor tier. To keep it, a builder has to install a lot of TimberTech and do it to TimberTech's standards. For you, it means:</p>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>A crew that knows TimberTech gapping, fastening and framing requirements, so your warranty holds.</li>
    <li>Manufacturer-backed labor and material warranty coverage on qualifying projects, in addition to our 7-year workmanship warranty.</li>
    <li>Access to the full TimberTech lineup, including decking, railing, HideAway privacy screens and lighting.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>See all of our manufacturer credentials on the <a href="/certified-pro-installer">certified Pro Installer page</a>.</p>

  <h2>TimberTech lines we install</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li><strong>Good:</strong> Prime+, Premier, Terrain, Terrain+</li>
    <li><strong>Better:</strong> Harvest, Harvest+, Landmark, Reserve</li>
    <li><strong>Best:</strong> Legacy and Vintage collections</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Browse colors and see them on finished decks in our <a href="/design-ideas/composite-decking">decking &amp; colors guide</a>, or read Levi's take on <a href="/blog/is-higher-end-pvc-decking-worth-it">whether higher-end PVC is worth it</a>.</p>

  <h2>Recent TimberTech decks we built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#highland-english-walnut-hideaway">Highland:</a> Vintage English Walnut around two hot tubs, with HideAway privacy screens and recessed step lights.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#highland-legacy-pecan-covered">Highland:</a> Legacy Pecan under a vaulted gable roof with stone columns.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#pleasant-grove-foothills-french-white-oak">Pleasant Grove foothills:</a> French White Oak with illuminated glass railing.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#saratoga-springs-dark-cocoa">Saratoga Springs:</a> Coconut Husk with a Dark Cocoa picture-frame border and Fortress railing.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#sandy-weathered-teak">Sandy:</a> Weathered Teak on a covered second-story deck.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#sundance-cabin-english-walnut">Sundance:</a> English Walnut cabin deck with a waterfall bench, sauna and hot tub.</li>
    <li><a href="/project-showcase#draper-brownstone-slate-gray">Draper:</a> Slate Gray with a Brownstone border and built-in bench.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="grid grid-2">
    <Photo sizes="grid-3" src="/images/projects/pleasant-grove-foothills-french-white-oak/french-white-oak-picture-frame-border-detail" alt="TimberTech French White Oak decking with a picture-frame border" />
    <Photo sizes="grid-3" src="/images/projects/highland-legacy-pecan-covered/timbertech-legacy-pecan-board-texture-closeup" alt="Close-up of TimberTech Legacy Pecan deck boards" />
  </div>

  <h2>Watch a TimberTech deck go in</h2>
  <p>This Lehi rebuild uses TimberTech Dark Cocoa boards with hidden fasteners, Fortress railing and built-in stair lights, from tear-out to the lights coming on at dusk.</p>
  <YouTubeVideo video={videos.lehiRebuildShort} caption="TimberTech Dark Cocoa deck rebuild in Lehi, Utah by TC Decks." />

  <h2>Under the boards</h2>
  <p>Great decking deserves a frame that lasts as long. We often build TimberTech decks on <a href="/steel-deck-framing">Fortress steel framing</a> or <a href="/oc-lumber">OC Lumber</a>, and when a project uses wood we protect the joists with flashing tape. Read the <a href="/design-ideas/built-to-last">built-to-last guide</a> for the details.</p>
  <p>Planning a TimberTech deck? <a href="/contact">Call for a free estimate</a> and we'll talk through lines, colors and layout on the phone.</p>
</Service>
